---
description: Rules for Laravel controllers and Blade views in MarineCaddie
globs: app/Http/Controllers/**/*.php,resources/views/**/*.blade.php
alwaysApply: false
---

# Controller Rules

## index() method structure
```php
$hideInactive = $request->boolean('hide_inactive', false); // default false

$items = Model::query()
    ->when($search, fn($q) => $q->where('col', 'like', ListSearch::contains($search)))
    ->when($hideInactive, fn($q) => $q->where('is_active', 1))
    ->paginate(25);

if ($request->ajax()) {
    return response()->json([
        'html'       => view('Module.partials.rows', compact('items'))->render(),
        'pagination' => (string) $items->links(),
        'total'      => $items->total(),
    ]);
}
return view('Module.index', compact('items'));
```

## File operations
Always use `PrivateDisk::delete($path)` — never `Storage::delete()` directly.

# Blade Rules

## partials/rows.blade.php
- Only `<tr>` tags — no `<table>` or `<tbody>`
- `@empty` row `colspan` must equal thead `<th>` count exactly
- `{{ $var }}` auto-escapes — safe for output

## JS in Blade
- Use `bindAjaxListFilters()` from shared partial for all list pages
- DataTables `columnDefs.targets` must be integer, not array
- After `table.destroy()` — reinitialize from scratch, never reuse old instance
